  "reason": "Evidence: The top three configs (0.725, 0.721, 0.713) all use scvi_n200 + transformer aggregation, confirming this as the dominant architecture. Within this sub-space, imagenet_vit_l + weighted is the best (0.725), but resnet50 showed a notably higher F1 (0.695 vs 0.685) suggesting more balanced predictions. Question: config_002 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) is the last untested multiprofile+transformer+scvi_n200 combination, testing whether concat fusion synergizes with resnet50's representation in a way that might close or exceed the 0.725 mark. Rationale: With 3 experiments remaining, completing this critical sub-space is the highest-value exploration; it has the highest expected accuracy among untested multiprofile configs (~0.71–0.72) and will clarify whether the small accuracy gap between image encoders is offset by fusion choice. Expected cost: ~6 GPU hours (comparable to config_049 with resnet50+transformer), making it moderately expensive but justified by its position in the most promising architectural family."
